  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "correctness",
    "affected_api": null,
    "observed_behavior": "For timedelta64 groupby sums, values that should overflow instead silently wrap to an unrelated Timedelta value; and for certain skipna=False cases a group's result can be incorrectly truncated to NaT (missing).",
    "expected_behavior": "Overflow in timedelta operation should raise OutOfBoundsTimedelta(\"overflow in timedelta operation\"); and for skipna=False the result should not be misidentified as NA when the running total merely passes through NPY_NAT\u2014e.g. a group that should sum to -1 ns should return -1 ns rather than NaT.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "Series([Timedelta.max] * 2).groupby([0, 0]).sum() (then indexing [0])",
      "Series([Timedelta.min, Timedelta(-1, \"ns\"), Timedelta.max]).groupby([0, 0, 0]).sum(skipna=False) (then indexing [0])"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "Series([Timedelta.max] * 2).groupby([0, 0]).sum()[0]",
        "buggy_output": "Timedelta('-1 days +23:59:59.999999998')",
        "expected_output": "OutOfBoundsTimedelta: overflow in timedelta operation",
        "value_kind": "exception",
        "source": "pr_body:PR#66587 sim=0.618; pr_body:PR#66587 sim=0.586"
      },
      {
        "input": "Series([Timedelta.min, Timedelta(-1, \"ns\"), Timedelta.max]).groupby([0, 0, 0]).sum(skipna=False)[0]",
        "buggy_output": "NaT",
        "expected_output": "-1 ns",
        "value_kind": "string",
        "source": "pr_body:PR#66587 sim=0.615; pr_body:PR#66587 sim=0.615"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "Observed wrong numeric Timedelta output for groupby sum: Timedelta('-1 days +23:59:59.999999998').",
      "Expected behavior for that case: Series([Timedelta.max] * 2).sum() raises OutOfBoundsTimedelta(\"overflow in timedelta operation\") (since GH-43178, stated in PR text).",
      "When skipna=False, the bug is that NA-ness of a group was decided by testing whether the running total equals NPY_NAT; this cannot distinguish a real NaT from a partial sum that passes through the sentinel, leading to silent truncation. The example should yield -1 ns instead of NaT.",
      "The PR text describes that int64 addition is modular and a net carry is tracked; representability is checked via whether the carry is back to zero, and also considers NPY_NAT as part of the representability check."
    ]
  },
